  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase changes: 823 K, melting point of $Sb_{2}S_{3}$ ; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 9.714$ kcal/mol. \n903.9 K, melting point of Sb; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.750$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td>298.15-823 K:</td><td> $Cp^o$  = 25.971 + 9.160x $10^{-3}$ T - 0.046x $10^5$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">823-1050 K:</td><td> $H^o-H_2^o_{98}$  = 25.971x $10^{-3}$ T + 4.580x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 0.046x $10^2$ T $^{-1}$  - 8.166 $Cp^o$  = 69.133 - 25.366x $10^{-3}$ T - 1.662x $10^5$ T $^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o-H_2^o_{98}$  = 69.133x $10^{-3}$ T - 12.683x $10^{-6}$ T $^2$  + 1.662x $10^2$ T $^{-1}$  - 22.478</td></tr></table>\nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-823 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -80.906 + 3.280 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} + 1.756 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 54.650 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -80.906 - 3.280 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln \\text{T} - 1.756 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} - 27.325 \\text{T}^{-1} + 82.690 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">823-903.9 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -95.218 + 46.443 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 15.507 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 106.950 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -95.218 - 46.443 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln \\text{T} + 15.507 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 53.475 \\text{T}^{-1} + 375.498 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">903.9-1050 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -102.225 + 41.619 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 13.163 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 63.750 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -102.225 - 41.619 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln \\text{T} + 13.163 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 31.875 \\text{T}^{-1} + 352.560 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K and high-temperature data from Johnson (56). Low-temperature heat capacities and entropy at 298 from King (68). ",
